      "reasons": [
        "The definition says development is from “before birth through adulthood and later years,” but the packet only explicitly specifies prenatal bonding/maternal-fetal attachment and then “adult partnerships and intergenerational caregiving”; it does not explicitly mention “later years.”",
        "The phrase “whole course of human life” is broader than what the packet explicitly states; the packet supports that relational contexts persist “throughout the lifespan,” but does not separately support the claim framed as a complete course across all named life phases (especially “later years”)."
